Marcel Holtmann wrote:

| thanks for your information and if this device uses security mode 3 by
| default, my stomach is turning up-side-down. I don't know what stupid
| software engineers this mobile phone manufactures hire, but pairing for
| a vCard exchange is bad. After that you can use every service of that
| mobile phone. Do they ever read any security papers :(
|

I don't know what those people do, but what's in the media is really
astonishing - and bad news mostly. I always wanted to get a BT mobile to
use my BT headset and stuff, but I won't until the security measures
that are defined in the BT specs are implemented at least a tiny bit by
the mobile phone producers. I agree with Andreas who thinks that most
"problems" are based on managment decisions that do not understand how
BT is supposed to work.

I hope that at some point in the future a Linux-based Smartphone with
bluez or something alike will emerge, so that at least a little bit of
programmers heart and soul resides in the device.

regards,
~  Lars
